On the home page, the grey text under the headings is now #3d4650. The 16 functional tests pass. I didn't look at the page in a browser.

I added a rule in `site/css/pages.css`, at the start of the Home section:

```css
.page-home {
  --color-muted: #3d4650;
}
```

It overrides the shared muted-grey colour only on pages with `<body class="page-home">`, so the other five pages are unchanged. That covers the hero lede, the card descriptions (Aurora Lamp, the three "Why Acme" perks, the newsletter blurb) and the stat labels. It also covers the small "We never share your address." note under the signup form, which uses the same grey.

